„­bible_version£KJV¤book)§chapter¨sections›…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶And it came to pass on the second sabbath after the first, that he went through the corn fields; and his disciples plucked the ears of corn, and did eat, rubbing them in their hands.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd certain of the Pharisees said unto them, Why do ye that which is not lawful to do on the sabbath days?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹And Jesus answering them said, Have ye not read so much as this, what David did, when himself was an hungred, and they which were with him;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©how he went into the house of God, and did take and eat the shewbread, and gave also to them that were with him; which it is not lawful to eat but for the priests alone?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙGAnd he said unto them, That the Son of man is Lord also of the sabbath.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book)§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd it came to pass also on another sabbath, that he entered into the synagogue and taught: and there was a man whose right hand was withered.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ„And the scribes and Pharisees watched him, whether he would heal on the sabbath day; that they might find an accusation against him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘But he knew their thoughts, and said to the man which had the withered hand, Rise up, and stand forth in the midst. And he arose and stood forth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThen said Jesus unto them, I will ask you one thing; Is it lawful on the sabbath days to do good, or to do evil? to save life, or to destroy it?¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
